WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:23.000
Inspect the powers, preserve the substitution factor, and use an identity on everything else.

00:23.000 --> 00:48.000
Odd sine saves sine x. Odd cosine saves cosine x. If both powers are even, use half-angle identities.

00:48.000 --> 01:12.000
For sine cubed x times cosine to the four thirds x, save one sine and use u equal to cosine x.

01:12.000 --> 01:40.000
Even powers call for half angles. An odd cosine power calls for u equal to sine x.

01:40.000 --> 02:06.000
Even secant saves secant squared for u equal to tangent. Odd tangent saves secant tangent for u equal to secant.

02:06.000 --> 02:30.000
Use tangent squared equals secant squared minus one, or save secant squared and substitute tangent.

02:30.000 --> 03:01.000
Match each remaining secant and tangent integral to its preserved derivative factor, then differentiate to verify.

03:01.000 --> 03:27.000
For products with different angles, convert products to sums before integrating.

03:27.000 --> 03:53.000
Apply product-to-sum, then track the inner-frequency factor during integration.

03:53.000 --> 04:17.000
Classify, preserve a derivative pair, apply one identity, integrate, and verify.
